       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is above the safe limit for acetaminophen.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 2000 mg three times daily is 6,000 mg/day. The usual maximum for a healthy adult is 4,000 mg/day, and many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 2000 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg. At 70 kg, the weight-based ceiling is about 15 mg/kg, or roughly 1,050 mg.\n- **Risk:** This regimen risks hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 1000 mg by mouth three times daily (3,000 mg/day)\n- 1000 mg by mouth four times daily (4,000 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 650 mg by mouth every 6 hours\n\nIf you do want 2000 mg three times daily, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note. I'd rather you confirm that explicitly than have me enter it as written."
